(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-glass-forming-decision :authorize-glass-forming-operation :proceed-with-glass-forming-operation :finalize-glass-cutting-decision :authorize-glass-cutting-operation :proceed-with-glass-cutting-operation :override-workshop-safety-officer-judgment :override-safety-officer-judgment)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/related (vector "2799007211-cloud-itonami-isco-7211-metal-moulders-coremakers-coverage" "2799007125-cloud-itonami-isco-7125-glaziers-coverage" "2799009311-cloud-itonami-isco-9311-mining-quarrying-labourers-coverage")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "proceed with the glass-forming operation" "proceed with the glass forming operation" "authorize the glass-forming operation" "authorize the glass forming operation" "proceed with the glass-cutting operation" "proceed with the glass cutting operation" "authorize the glass-cutting operation" "authorize the glass cutting operation" "finalize the glass-forming decision" "finalize the glass-cutting decision" "override the workshop safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override workshop safety officer judgment")), (:adr/id 2799007315), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}"), (:actor/domain :manufacturing/glass-workshop-scheduling-logistics-coordination), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :glassworker-verified :workshop-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "7315"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799007315: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7315 Glass Makers, Cutters, Grinders and Finishers glass-workshop scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7315\n-- Glass Makers, Cutters, Grinders and Finishers** only, Wave3\n(production/trades) of the rollout (Wave0/1/2 100% complete, Wave3\nbatches 1-5 already landed: construction/metal trades 7111-7224, all\nagriculture classes).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7315\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-occupation\n\\\"7315\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/technology`\nsibling present at the correct `../technology` relative path), and its\n`:name` read exactly \"Glass Makers, Cutters, Grinders and Finishers\"\n-- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's\n`:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics\n:identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository\nexisted at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7315` (`gh api` 404\nconfirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry\nedit promote the `7315` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nGlass makers, cutters, grinders and finishers work with high-temperature\nglass furnaces and sharp glass materials -- real physical-safety\nstakes (burn exposure from furnace/molten-glass handling, cut hazards\nfrom sharp/broken glass, and grinding-dust/respiratory hazards from\nfinishing work). The controlling constraint for this vertical is that\nthe closed op allowlist must NEVER include any op that directly\nfinalizes a glass-forming/cutting-execution decision, or overrides a\nworkshop safety officer's judgment -- those decisions must always be a\nhard permanent block or an always-escalate op, never auto-commit-\neligible. This actor is deliberately scoped to GLASS-WORKSHOP\nSCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION ONLY -- it never performs\nglass-forming, -cutting, -grinding or -finishing work itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7211`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7211)\n(Metal Moulders and Coremakers: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor`\nsplit, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set, same wave, closest\nanalogous hot-process/heat-exposure workshop safety pattern) -- cloned\nand read in full in this session.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7315` as an OSS\nglass-workshop scheduling/logistics-coordination actor for glass\nmakers, cutters, grinders and finishers, following the SAME\ngoverned-actor architecture as every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*`\nactor in this fleet: **Glass Workshop Coordination Advisor ⊣\nGlassCoordGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph\n(`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned identically to the\nreference's `deps.edn` -- a different library coordinate from the\n`langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*` actor family),\nwith an independent Governor, human-in-the-loop approval via\n`interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **glass-workshop scheduling/logistics\ncoordination ONLY, never direct glass-forming/cutting-execution\nauthority** -- it must NEVER be designed to exercise, simulate\nexercising, or propose exercising a glass-forming/cutting-execution\ndecision, or any override of a workshop safety officer's judgment.\nThese are not merely gated behind escalation -- they are structurally\nabsent from the op-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- task/materials-usage/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task/furnace-schedule scheduling\n  proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a burn-hazard/cut-hazard/\n  furnace-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit\n  eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- glass-materials procurement proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\nglass-forming/cutting-execution decision or a workshop-safety-officer-\njudgment override. These are **structurally absent from the\nop-allowlist entirely**, not merely gated behind escalation -- an op\nsuch as `:finalize-glass-forming-decision` cannot even be proposed by\nthe reference mock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions only\never emit one of the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a\nforged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever\nproduced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD check\n(`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently. A second,\nindependent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-action`) names eight\nconcretely-forbidden ops (`glasscoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-glass-forming-decision`, `:authorize-glass-forming-operation`,\n`:proceed-with-glass-forming-operation`, `:finalize-glass-cutting-decision`,\n`:authorize-glass-cutting-operation`, `:proceed-with-glass-cutting-operation`,\n`:override-workshop-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`glasscoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-glass-forming-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-glass-forming-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-glass-cutting-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-workshop-safety-officer-judgment`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Glassworker unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered glassworker record (`:no-glassworker`).\n   Never trusts the proposal's own claim of who the glassworker is.\n2. **Workshop unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an\n   independently registered glass workshop site (`:no-workshop`).\n   Together with check 1, this directly implements the CRITICAL\n   invariant that a worker/workshop record must be independently\n   verified/registered before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the eight\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with a\n   glass-forming or glass-cutting operation, or overriding a workshop\n   safety officer's judgment, is a second HARD, PERMANENT block\n   (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated unconditionally on content --\n   defense-in-depth on top of the allowlist check: even if a future\n   change somehow widened the allowlist, content-based rejection still\n   independently blocks glass-forming/cutting-execution/safety-override\n   language wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a burn-hazard/cut-hazard/\n  furnace-condition observation -- it never resolves the concern\n  itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is the hazard data,\"\n  never \"here is what I recommend doing about workshop safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  glass-materials order is not itself unsafe, unlike a\n  glass-forming/cutting-execution or safety-officer-override attempt,\n  which is why it is handled by a different mechanism (soft escalate\n  vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"glass\", \"furnace\", \"safety\") can accidentally match inside the mock\nadvisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly the risk\nthis vertical's own vocabulary (a glass-workshop coordination actor\nworking adjacent to glass-forming/cutting work necessarily discusses\nthose concepts to do its scheduling/logging job) could trigger if\nphrased carelessly. `glasscoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is\nphrased exclusively as finalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"proceed\nwith the glass-forming operation\", \"authorize the glass-cutting\noperation\", \"override the workshop safety officer's judgment\" --\nmatching the task's own worked example phrasing), never bare nouns,\nand\n`glasscoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for glassworker ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for\nglass-finishing task ...\", \"... routed for workshop safety officer\nreview\") WITHOUT containing any of the full finalization-action\nphrases, so the regression test is a genuine stress test of the\nbare-noun-vs-action-phrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on\nfirst run in this session -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard\nitself was never tripped during development.\n`glasscoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nadditionally exercises the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7315\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7315` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7315`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 21 tests, 45 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-glass-forming-batch` that is\n  merely gated behind an always-escalate list (the shape\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`):\n  rejected outright per the task's explicit domain-design guidance --\n  an always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize a\n  glass-forming/cutting-execution decision exists in the code path and\n  is merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision this severe\n  (furnace burn exposure, sharp-glass cut hazards), the capability\n  itself must not exist. The only op related to workshop-safety\n  escalation is `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces the need for\n  human/workshop-safety-officer attention and never itself decides,\n  authorizes, or defers a glass-forming/cutting-execution decision for\n  later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the 3313\n  reference's transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check): rejected per the\n  task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold glass-materials\n  order is not itself unsafe, so it is handled as a soft escalate\n  gate, not a hard block; only the glass-forming/cutting-execution/\n  safety-officer-override class is a hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"glass\" \"furnace\"\n  \"safety\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked example for this\n  exact task), and per the explicit instruction to phrase\n  scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare\n  nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses glass/\n  furnace/safety-officer concepts to do its scheduling/logging job, so\n  a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking the actor's own legitimate\n  proposals (regression-tested directly against rationale text that\n  deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Naming the excluded-op set after \"workshop safety officer\" only,\n  vs. also naming a second distinct authority figure (mirroring house\n  building's dual safety-officer/foreman split): rejected -- the\n  task's domain design names only \"a workshop-safety officer's\n  judgment\" as the authority figure for this vertical, so a single\n  `:override-workshop-safety-officer-judgment` op (plus a generic\n  `:override-safety-officer-judgment` alias and matching phrase\n  variants) fully covers the specified scope without inventing an\n  unspecified second authority role.\n- Merging `glassworker` and `workshop` into a single entity (only\n  checking one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity\n  provenance shape (independently-registered glassworker AND\n  independently-registered workshop) matches the CRITICAL invariant\n  that a \"worker/workshop record must be independently verified/\n  registered before any action\" and the established pattern from\n  prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors with two-sided provenance\n  checks.\n- Splitting glass-forming and glass-cutting into two separately-named\n  op families in the scope-excluded set (rather than a single unified\n  \"glass-forming/cutting-execution\" concept): kept the split (eight\n  ops instead of six, mirroring both \"forming\" and \"cutting\" verbs)\n  because ISCO-08 7315 explicitly covers Glass Makers (forming),\n  Cutters, Grinders and Finishers (cutting/finishing) as one unit\n  group, and both categories of physical execution decision carry\n  distinct hazard profiles (furnace burn exposure vs. sharp-glass cut\n  hazard) that the task's CRITICAL note calls out separately --\n  neither should be underspecified relative to the other.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- task/materials-usage/progress data\n   logging only. Requires an independently registered glassworker AND\n   workshop (`:no-glassworker`/`:no-workshop`). Not a\n   glass-forming/cutting-execution or safety-officer decision in any\n   respect -- it is a records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task/furnace-schedule\n   scheduling proposal only. Cannot carry a glass-forming/cutting-\n   execution decision (structurally absent from the op's field shape;\n   any such attempt via free text is caught by the\n   `:scope-excluded-action` content check). Does not authorize,\n   finalize, or draw any conclusion about a specific forming or\n   cutting operation -- it is a calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a burn-hazard/cut-hazard/\n   furnace-condition concern to a human/workshop safety officer;\n   ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence level, NEVER\n   auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through which a\n   safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself -- the workshop\n   safety officer reviews and acts entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- glass-materials procurement\n   proposal only (item, cost). Not a glass-forming/cutting-execution\n   or authorization decision of any kind -- it is a\n   purchasing-logistics action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling\n   escalation (above 2000 always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na glass-forming/cutting-execution decision (e.g. proceeding with a\nspecific glass-forming or glass-cutting operation) or a\nworkshop-safety-officer-judgment override -- these categories are\nstructurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op\nallowlist itself (`glasscoord.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) eight\nconcretely-named forbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit\nlevel (`glasscoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`glasscoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-glass-forming-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-glass-forming-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-glass-cutting-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-workshop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`glasscoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with a glass-forming operation or override a\nworkshop safety officer's judgment even via an otherwise-allowlisted\nop\n(`glasscoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-workshop-safety-officer`).\n"), (:adr/date "2026-07-18"), (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}"), (:test/counts "{:total 21, :assertions 45, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "Glass Workshop Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice"), (:db/id -1), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :glassworker-verification :workshop-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7315"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7315"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7315)), (:test/simulator :glasscoord.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7315 — Glass Makers, Cutters, Grinders and Finishers Glass Workshop Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7315)))
